  "content": {
    "title": "Why is UCLA coach Cori Close wearing leather pants vs South Carolina in NCAA championship?",
    "text": "Updated April 5, 2026, 4:00 p.m. ETUCLA women's basketball coach Cori Close may not typically be superstitious, but she's not taking any chances in the NCAA Tournament championship game.Close is sporting black leather pants for the title game between her No. 1 seed Bruins (36-1) and No. 1 seed South Carolina (36-3) at Mortgage Matchup Center in Phoenix on April 5 (3:30 p.m. ET, ABC).The pants are the same ones Close wore in the Sweet 16 against No. 4 seed Minnesota. The Bruins won that game 80-56 to advance to the Elite Eight, for just the third time under Close.\"I'm not superstitious at all, but I guess it is a little bit by popular demand,\" Close told ESPN's Holly Rowe on the pregame show on April 5. \"Several people said to me, 'I'm just so glad you won (in the Final Four) because what if it had been because you didn't have the leather pants on in the semifinals.' So hey, we're giving the people what they want. As my strength coach would say, leather up, coach.\"On March 29, Close said on the \"Welcome to the Party Show\" hosted by Abby Wambach, Julie Foudy and Billie Jean King that the superstition around the pants was started by strength coach Ash Samaniego in Paris, France, before the 2024-25 season opener. The Bruins beat Louisville, and since, Close said she is undefeated when wearing the pants.Tia Reid covers Jackson State sports for theClarion Ledger. Email her attreid@usatodayco.com and follow her on X @tiareid65.",
